The concept of Social Welfare encompasses wider social pro- tection in the form of social welfare which includes: subsidised housing, employment aids, and welfare benefits. Child abuse co-exists in a large proportion of situations in which women are subjected to intimate partner violence, and child protec- tion is increasingly annexed with victim interventions. There- fore in this section estimating the costs of social welfare the following costs are addressed:

Housing Aid;

Financial Assistance;

Child Protection and Family Support.

